From 0df2814e6154e3861daccaf8297a7a94a3f9bf83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiro836 <17294277+Shiro836@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:39:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/26] hwcomposer: the Android display follows the window,
 through a display reconnect sent from its own thread
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With Waydroid's hwc2on1 "Handle primary hotplugs" patch, an HWC1
hotplug(0, 1) makes SurfaceFlinger re-read the primary display's configs and
recreate the display, which is how upstream 40c54a5 ("Call hotplug on display
resize") lets Android's display size follow the window. Upstream sends it from
hwc_set(); that is the SurfaceFlinger crash patch 0016 removed (the callback
lands on SurfaceFlinger's main thread inside presentAndGetReleaseFences).

Sent from any other thread, SurfaceFlinger queues the event and handles it at
its next commit (onComposerHalHotplug -> commitTransactionsLocked ->
processDisplayHotplugEventsLocked), but the stock composer 2.1 HAL is then not
safe: the adapter takes its state mutex and the Display's mutex in the
opposite order to validate()/present(), and ComposerClient frees the display's
cached buffer handles while the old layers can still be presented. A vendor
image whose composer HAL fixes both declares
ro.vendor.composer.safe_primary_reconnect=true.

With that property:
- display-resize.cpp owns a resize thread. A configure that changes the size
  publishes the new touch range at once and arms the thread; once the window
  has not changed for persist.waydroid.resize_settle_ms (default 250, as
  Waydroid's lineage-23.2 hwcomposer), the thread makes floor(window *
  output scale) the display's only config and calls procs->hotplug(0, 1),
  then invalidate. It holds no lock of this module while it calls out
  (modes_mutex and resize_mutex are released first).
- The display has one mode, the window's size; the aspect ladder and
  set-user-preferred-display-mode are only used without the property.
- Only the full-UI window (task "0") drives the display size; per-app
  windows of the multi-window modes keep the old path.
- A forced size left by an earlier session is cleared once, as on the
  fullscreen path, so the logical display follows too.
- A decorated window keeps its scaled view while the size settles and is
  presented 1:1 again once the guest display has the window's size.
Without the property nothing changes: no hotplug is sent and the display
keeps its calibrated size and mode ladder. create_display() logs which of the
two paths is active.

modes, active_mode and phys_width/phys_height are now guarded by
modes_mutex (a leaf lock): the resize thread replaces them while composer
threads read them in getDisplayConfigs/getDisplayAttributes/setActiveConfig.

The poison guard stays in hwcomposer.cpp and wayland-hwc.cpp, so no code in
the present path or on the Wayland thread can call hotplug; the one caller in
display-resize.cpp aborts unless it runs on the resize thread.

复用 ATV 的窗口几何所有权和 250ms settle 语义，将已有 resize worker 移入 display-resize.cpp，避免两套线程；只有 ro.vendor.composer.safe_primary_reconnect=true 才发主显示重连。配置保持 ATV 单一 config，尺寸通过 modes_mutex 保护，在 settle 后更新；保留每连接窗口、task streams 与触摸范围即时更新，不引入 A13 模式阶梯或 cmd window size。Soong 同时编入 prime-copy.cpp 和 display-resize.cpp。

(cherry picked from commit 7880ca3492a94bfb267c95954d19c94d8ccb5720)
